<section class="section migration-section"><div class="shell split-panel"><div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">A migration path, not a cliff</p><h2>Import your Evernote archive.</h2><p>Export notebooks from Evernote as ENEX files, then upload them from DocManFu’s admin import screen. Imports run in the background and retain tags, creation dates, plain-text note content, and supported attachment files. Attachments are represented as independent documents.</p><ol class="number-list"><li><span>1</span>Export one or more notebooks as ENEX</li><li><span>2</span>Upload the ENEX file in DocManFu</li><li><span>3</span>Review imported documents and processing jobs</li><li><span>4</span>Keep your export as an independent backup</li></ol></div><div class="migration-card reveal delay-1"><div class="migration-source"><span>Legacy archive</span><b>Personal Documents.enex</b><small>1,248 notes · 9.6 GB</small></div><div class="migration-arrow">→</div><div class="migration-destination"><img src="/assets/images/logo-mark.png" alt=""><span>DocManFu</span><b>Imported and searchable</b><small>Tags · creation dates · text · attachment files</small></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section faq-section"><div class="shell narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Migration questions</p><h2>Before you cancel anything.</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Does DocManFu replace every Evernote feature?</summary><p>No. It is purpose-built for personal document storage rather than general note-taking, tasks, team collaboration, or web clipping. If your primary use is archiving PDFs, scans, statements, and records, that focus is an advantage.</p></details><details><summary>Should I keep the ENEX export?</summary><p>Yes. Preserve the original export as a backup until you have verified important notes and attachments in DocManFu. Caution is inexpensive; regret has premium pricing.</p></details><details><summary>Can I run AI locally?</summary><p>Yes. Configure Ollama to keep compatible AI analysis local, or disable AI entirely. OCR and search still work.</p></details></div></div></section>
